SUMMARY:20s & 30s Renaissance Festival Camping Trip
LOCATION:Parking lot\, 5 Pine S\nCarver\, MA 02330
DESCRIPTION:Friday\, September 25\, 2026 | 5:00 PM\nhttps://activities.out
 doors.org/s/oc-activity/a5UVX000001FiWP2A0/\nHear ye! Hear ye! Embraceth a
 dventure and occasions of socialization most joyous!WE'RE GOING TO THE REN
 AISSANCE FESTIVAL\, PEASANTS!!! WOOOO-ETH!!!Join your fellow 20s & 30s for
  a Ren-Fest camp out the weekend of September 25-27. We have a group camps
 ite reserved at Myles Standish State Forest for camping Friday and Saturda
 y night thus enabling easy access to King Richard's Faire in Carver\, MA o
 n Saturday\, September 26!20s & 30s folx from any chapter are welcome to j
 oin us on this jaunt\, fealty to the Worcester Chapter is not a pre-requis
 ite. Camping will be capped at 20 people (campsite regulation) but for any
 one unable to join us for camping\, all are still welcome to come meet up 
 with us at King Richard's Faire for a day of festivities.Several items of 
 note:Members of the Jackalope Society will be given one week registration 
 preference (August 30 - September 5)\, after that it'll be first come firs
 t serve to register.If you're looking to just camp but not Ren-Fest\, this
  event is not for you and we recommend looking for tenting elsewhere. Come
  ready to revel renaissance style.You must secure your own ticket to King 
 Richard's Faire! It can sell out\, so we recommend getting that ticket as 
 soon as you're confirmed for this camp out (www.kingrichardsfaire.net). Ti
 ckets are $40 for September 26.No meals will be provided on this camping t
 rip\, however the Worcester Gear Shed can provide camp equipment. Cost for
  the campsite is pay what you can ($5 is appreciated).Costumes for the Kin
 g Richard's Faire are encouraged but not required! If you'd like to borrow
  or need some tips\, your fearless leader is a massive nerd and can offer 
 budget friendly recommendations.
END:VEVENT
