SUMMARY:Annual Maine House Autumn Spectacular
LOCATION:Bryant Pond\nWoodstock\, ME
DESCRIPTION:Friday\, October 9\, 2026 | 12:00 PM\nhttps://activities.outdo
 ors.org/s/oc-activity/a5UVX000001D6F72AK/\n You are cordially invited to 
 join the Worcester Chapter for our 33rd anniversary trip to Western Maine 
 to enjoy the gorgeous autumn colors of Maine over Columbus Day weekend. We
 'll be staying at the Maine House\, located on the shore of beautiful Lake
  Christopher in the village of Bryant Pond. The charming historic house wi
 ll be the base for our many hikes and other outdoor activities. The Maine 
 House has cozy private rooms for couples and comfy bunks for singles. The 
 dining area has a panoramic view over the lake\, and a large living room w
 ith a fireplace invites all to relax and socialize during the evening. In 
 addition\, there is a hot tub and a steam room to help you recover after y
 our day of activities. Paddle right out the door on Lake Christopher in ca
 noes provided by the house. The trip fee includes three nights lodging (Fr
 i - Sun)\, three breakfasts and make-your-own-lunch buffets\, and two tast
 y dinners. Everyone helps with set-up or clean-up for a meal. With about 3
 0 people on the trip\, we will be able to offer various levels of hikes ea
 ch day\, ranging from easy to strenuous\, as well as other activities. We 
 will lead one road biking trip\, and there are nearby DIY paddling opportu
 nities. The trip cost this year is $175. Join us for this Worcester Chapte
 r classic which draws participants from all over the club.  
END:VEVENT
